{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Is not their cord pulled up</b> — Some interpret: the excess of their knowledge is pulled up and lost. Others said: for it is like יתרי פתח [my tent cords are stretched], that He tears their tent cords. And the one near to me: that it is like יתרה עשה [he made excess], which is wealth, and its meaning: that their wealth perishes in their death." "<b>They die, and not in wisdom</b> — Their wisdom is to amass wealth. This verse also teaches that man was created only to learn wisdom."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "Resolved the three prooftexts by their context: Job 4:21 (the lemma itself), Isaiah 54:2, and Ecclesiastes 2:6 respectively; Ibn Ezra cites them in abbreviated form."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:08.218709315Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}